Backend
  In your terminal, run:
  cd /Users/jonathanbeltran/service-center/backend
  source venv/bin/activate
  ADMIN_PASSWORD=yourpassword uvicorn main:app --reload
 You should see Uvicorn running on http://127.0.0.1:8000.

Frontend

  Open both files directly in your browser:
  - frontend/index.html — the worker shift picker
  - frontend/admin.html — the admin panel
How scheduling works
  1. Supervisor opens admin.html, sets the Scheduling Period (start and end dates).
     Every Monday-to-Sunday week in that range is opened for workers.
  2. Workers open index.html, pick their initials, and rank shifts for each week
     using the week tabs. Coming back later reloads what they already submitted.
  3. Days later, the supervisor opens admin.html, checks who has submitted, and
     clicks "Run Schedule for All Weeks". One schedule is produced per week and
     saved, so it is still there on the next visit.

Persistence
  All state (workers, shift sizes, period, submissions, results) is saved to a
  JSON file. Default: backend/store.json. Override with DATA_FILE.
  On Railway, attach a volume and set DATA_FILE=/data/store.json so submissions
  survive redeploys and restarts.
